# Fonts
# quattro's woff2-font-awesome maps to Fedora's fontawesome4-fonts + fontawesome-fonts-web.
# The JetBrainsMono Nerd Font the shell and terminals use has no Fedora package - it is installed
# from the nerd-fonts release by install/helpers/fedora-manual.sh. gnome-themes-extra was retired
# in Fedora 44 (the Yaru packages above cover GTK theming).
google-noto-fonts-common
google-noto-sans-fonts
google-noto-sans-cjk-fonts
google-noto-emoji-fonts
google-noto-color-emoji-fonts
jetbrains-mono-fonts
cascadia-mono-nf-fonts
fontawesome4-fonts
fontawesome-fonts-web
# ter-v16n, the console font install/config/console-font.sh sets on the TTY.
terminus-fonts-console

# Input Methods
fcitx5
fcitx5-gtk
fcitx5-qt5
fcitx5-qt6

# First-party tool runtime deps
# Shared libraries the first-party tools link against. The tools themselves are installed from
# upstream release binaries / source builds by install/helpers/fedora-first-party.sh, but their
# runtime dependencies are ordinary Fedora packages and belong here so dnf resolves them up front.
# (wtype, wl-clipboard and slurp - also first-party runtime deps - are already listed above.)
webkit2gtk4.1
gtk3
gtk-layer-shell
gstreamer1
gstreamer1-plugins-good
ffmpeg-free
alsa-lib
qt6-qtbase
qt6-qtdeclarative
qt6-qtmultimedia
hicolor-icon-theme
libadwaita
libepoxy
fontconfig
gtk4
xdg-desktop-portal
